                "evidence": "Cloudflare AI Search isn't billed yet. Billing starts on **2026-12-01**. Here's what you get after that:\n\n**Included each month**\n- 5M ingestion tokens\n- 10 GB-month of storage\n- 1,000 semantic queries\n- 1,000 full-text queries\n\n**Overage**\n- $0.75 per 1,000 hybrid queries\n- $0.10 per 1,000 full-text queries\n\n**Limits**\n- Up to 50 results per query\n- Up to 5 custom metadata fields per instance\n\nWhat it is: managed hybrid search (vector plus keyword) over built-in storage, R2 or a website crawl.\n\n**Gaps in the vault page:**\n- It calls the included queries \"semantic\" but prices overage as \"hybrid.\" It doesn't say whether those are the same thing.\n- It gives no overage rates for ingestion tokens or storage.\n- It doesn't say which Cloudflare plans the included amounts apply to.\n\nCheck those against Cloudflare's pricing page before you budget on them.\n\n**Source:** vault page [[Cloudflare AI Search]], reviewed 2026-11-01, built from `raw/2026-11/2026-11-01 cloudflare-ai-search-pricing`. Pricing pages count as fast-changing, so the vault treats a page as current for 30 days. This one is 6 days old, so I didn't search the web again and didn't change the vault.\n\nCoverage: vault only (1 page). Web, social and paid lanes weren't needed for a lookup the vault already answered. Spend: $0."
