                "evidence": "Cloudflare AI Search is free until **1 December 2026**, when billing starts. These figures come from my research vault ([[Cloudflare AI Search]]). That page was checked on 2026-11-01 against Cloudflare's pricing page and is within its 30-day freshness window, so I didn't search the web again.\n\n**Free each month:**\n- 5M ingestion tokens\n- 10 GB-month of storage\n- 1,000 semantic queries\n- 1,000 full-text queries\n\n**Cost beyond the free amounts:**\n- **$0.75 per 1,000 hybrid queries**\n- **$0.10 per 1,000 full-text queries**\n\n**Limits:**\n- Up to 50 results per query\n- Up to 5 custom metadata fields per instance\n\nThe free allowance mentions \"semantic\" queries, but the overage price is for \"hybrid\" queries. I think they mean the same thing (vector plus keyword search), but that's my assumption. Check Cloudflare's pricing page if the difference matters.\n\nThe vault page also doesn't give overage prices for ingestion tokens or storage. If you expect to go past 5M tokens or 10 GB, I can look those up on the web.\n\nCoverage: vault only, from one page reviewed 2026-11-01. I didn't search the web or social sources because the vault page was recent enough to cover the question."
