                ],
                "evidence": "Cloudflare AI Search has a monthly free allowance, and you only pay for usage above it. **Billing starts 2026-12-01.**\n\n**Included free each month:**\n- 5M ingestion tokens\n- 10 GB-month of storage\n- 1,000 semantic (vector) queries\n- 1,000 full-text (keyword) queries\n\n**Cost above the free amounts:**\n- $0.75 per 1,000 hybrid queries\n- $0.10 per 1,000 full-text queries\n\n**Limits that apply whatever you pay:**\n- Up to 50 results per query\n- Up to 5 custom metadata fields per instance\n\nOne thing is unclear. The free allowance is described as \"semantic queries\" but the overage is priced per \"hybrid query.\" The notes don't say whether those are the same thing, so check before you estimate costs for vector-heavy use. The notes also don't give a rate for ingestion or storage beyond the free amounts.\n\n**Source:** vault page `wiki/Cloudflare AI Search.md`, last reviewed 2026-11-01. It's based on Cloudflare's pricing page as captured on 2026-11-01 (`raw/2026-11/2026-11-01 cloudflare-ai-search-pricing`). Prices like these change often, so the page is treated as current for 30 days, and it's within that window. I took every figure from the vault page and didn't check the live page again. Re-check Cloudflare's pricing page before committing, especially near the December billing start.\n\nCoverage: vault only (one page, current). No web search, as the vault answered the question. Social lane not used. No paid spend."
